[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Configuration samples are installed in %%ETCDIR%%.

OpenJDK 21 or newer is required. To select another installed JDK, set
elasticsearch_java_home in /etc/rc.conf, for example:

elasticsearch_java_home="%%LOCALBASE%%/openjdk25"

Production bootstrap checks require at least 65535 open file descriptors.
Set the service login class's openfiles limit and kern.maxfilesperproc
accordingly; kern.maxfiles must also be large enough.

If bootstrap.memory_lock is enabled, allow sufficient locked memory and set
security.bsd.unprivileged_mlock=1. For a jail, enforce_statfs=1 is recommended.

Native machine learning is disabled on MidnightBSD. The BSD native backend
uses the system zstd library and BSD process resource limits for its sandbox.

Install plugins with the elasticsearch-plugin utility supplied by this port.
Package files are owned by root:wheel. Ensure plugin-created configuration
files and the elasticsearch.keystore are accessible to the elasticsearch user.
EOM
}
{ type: upgrade
  message: <<EOM
Elasticsearch 8.19 requires OpenJDK 21 or newer with this port's BSD native
backend. Review your service's elasticsearch_java_home setting before restart.

Before upgrading older 8.x installations, review the upstream 8.19 migration
notes, including AWS SDK v2 changes affecting EC2 discovery and S3 repositories:
https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/8.19/migrating-8.19.html

Upgrading to the current Elasticsearch 9 port requires passing through 8.19 first. Keep a
snapshot before any cluster upgrade; an in-place downgrade is unsupported.
EOM
}
]
